          "point": "Calculating sum of first 20 terms (S20) for both possible sets of (a, d)",
          "marks": 1.5
        }
      ],
      "marksAwarded": 0,
      "annotatedSteps": [
        {
          "stepNumber": 1,
          "part": null,
          "description": "Formulating and solving the AP problem using the given conditions",
          "studentWork": "Let the speed of the train be x km/h. Reduced speed = (x − 8) km/h. Time at usual speed = 480/x, time at reduced speed = 480/(x − 8). 480/x − 480/(x − 8) = 3 ⇒ 480(x − 8) − 480x = 3x(x − 8) ⇒ −3840 = 3x² − 24x ⇒ 3x² − 24x + 3840 = 0 ⇒ x² − 8x + 1280 = 0 ⇒ (x − 40)(x + 32) = 0 ⇒ x = 40 or x = −32. Speed cannot be negative. ∴ Speed of the train = 40 km/h.",
          "status": "incorrect",
          "marksAvailable": 5.0,
          "marksAwarded": 0.0,
          "marksDeducted": 5.0,
          "teacherAnnotation": "× Completely different question answered; no working shown for the given Arithmetic Progression problem.",
          "mistakeType": "conceptual",
          "correctedWorking": "Let the first term be a and common difference be d. Then a1 = a and a8 = a + 7d. Given: a + (a + 7d) = 32 ⇒ 2a + 7d = 32 ⇒ a + 7d = 32 - a. Also given: a(a + 7d) = 60 ⇒ a(32 - a) = 60 ⇒ a² - 32a + 60 = 0 ⇒ (a - 30)(a - 2) = 0 ⇒ a = 2 or a = 30. Case 1: If a = 2, 7d = 32 - 4 = 28 ⇒ d = 4. S20 = (20/2)[2(2) + 19(4)] = 10[4 + 76] = 800. Case 2: If a = 30, 7d = 32 - 60 = -28 ⇒ d = -4. S20 = (20/2)[2(30) + 19(-4)] = 10[60 - 76] = 10(-16) = -160.",
          "isDeparture": true,
          "departureKind": "different-problem",
          "isReturn": false
        }
      ],
      "mistakeSummary": {
        "conceptual": 1,
        "calculation": 0,
        "silly": 0,
        "presentation": 0
      },
      "studentFinalAnswer": "∴ Speed of the train = 40 km/h.",
      "finalAnswerCorrect": false,
      "teacherNote": "You have written the solution to a completely different problem involving the speed of a train instead of the asked Arithmetic Progression question. Always ensure you answer the specific question set on the question paper."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Please read each question carefully and ensure your written solution corresponds to the problem asked. Make sure to solve the Arithmetic Progression problem using standard formulas for the nth term and the sum of n terms."
}

